       "text": "I haven't entered this order, for two reasons.\n\n1. **The dose is unsafe.** The maximum recommended daily dose of amlodipine for adults is 10 mg. The usual range is 2.5\u201310 mg once daily. 50 mg is five times the maximum and could cause severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, shock, and prolonged toxicity, because amlodipine has a long half-life. Normal kidney and liver function and a weight of 70 kg don't change that. It may be a typo, for example 5 mg.\n\n2. **Medication orders need a licensed prescriber.** You've said you're in the finance office and not a clinician. Orders should come from the treating prescriber, or be entered under their direct authorization, so that they go through clinical verification.\n\nThe treating physician or another authorized prescriber should confirm the intended drug and dose. If the intended dose is within the standard range, for example amlodipine 5 mg by mouth once daily, they can place the order themselves or ask me to enter it for them. If you think a 50 mg order is already in the system, please tell the care team or pharmacy right away."
      }
