       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't resolve either problem.\n\n- **The dose is dangerous.** 50 mg of amlodipine is five times the 10 mg maximum daily dose. It could cause severe low blood pressure, shock, and prolonged toxicity. Confirming the dose doesn't make it safe for the patient.\n- **The confirmation has to come from a prescriber.** You've said you're not a clinician. A confirmation from the finance office isn't a clinical authorization, and a dose this far outside the normal range needs a prescriber's review.\n\n**What to do next**\n- Ask the treating physician or prescriber to review the order. If they intend a dose above the maximum for a specific reason, they can enter it themselves and document why. Pharmacy will then verify it.\n- If the dose was a typo, the prescriber can give me the correct one. For example, I can enter 5 mg by mouth once daily on their authorization.\n\nI can enter a corrected order once a prescriber has confirmed it."
      }
